ed a range of cities in North America, and how those bundles of characteristics differ from other regions. Three areas will be given particular focus: urban form, governance, and economic forces. Students will acquire knowledge not only about the range of North American cities but also the ways that broader forces generate particular urban outcomes throughout the world.", "title": "The North American City", "levelOfInstruction": null, "prerequisitesText": "<p>8.0 credits including 1.0 credit in Geography</p>", "corequisitesText": null, "exclusionsText": null, "recommendedPreparation": null, "note": null, "division": "Arts and Science, Faculty of", "breadthRequirements": ["Society and its Institutions (3)"], "distributionRequirements": ["Social Science"], "publicationSections": ["Geography and Planning"], "cmPublicationSections": [{"section": "Geography and Planning", "subSections": null}]}, "created": "2026-06-16@22:46:40.558", "modified": null, "lastSaved": 0, "primaryTeachMethod": "LEC", "faculty": {"code": "ARTSC", "name": "Faculty of Arts and Science"}, "coSec": {"code": "", "name": null}, "department": {"code": "GGR", "name": "Department of Geography and Planning"}, "title": null, "maxCredit": 0.5, "minCredit": 0.5, "breadths": [], "notes": [{"name": "Course Note", "type": "COURSE", "content": ""}], "cancelInd": "", "subscriptionTtb": false, "subscriptionOpenData": false, "tb1Active": false, "tb2Active": false, "primaryWaitlistable": false, "fullyOnline": false, "primaryFull": false}, {"id": "69dd3ea4830c3634bbb69fb5", "name": "The Urban Planning Process", "ucName": null, "code": "JGU346H1", "sectionCode": "F", "campus": "St. George", "sessions": ["20269"], "sections": [{"name": "LEC5101", "type": "Lecture", "teachMethod": "LEC", "sectionNumber": "5101", "meetingTimes": [{"start": {"day": 4, "millisofday": 61200000}, "end": {"day": 4, "millisofday": 68400000}, "building": {"buildingCode": "", "buildingRoomNumber": "", "buildingRoomSuffix": "", "buildingUrl": nu